5
00:00:11,181 --> 00:00:13,574
[Episode 2]

6
00:00:19,141 --> 00:00:21,014
Yeah, hello?

7
00:00:21,014 --> 00:00:22,448
I just got here.

8
00:00:22,448 --> 00:00:25,781
What floor was it again?
Has forensics arrived?

9
00:01:16,581 --> 00:01:18,581
- You're here?
- Yeah.

10
00:01:24,648 --> 00:01:28,548
The bullet went straight through his temple.
Death was instantaneous.

11
00:01:28,548 --> 00:01:30,381
Have you identified the victim?

12
00:01:30,381 --> 00:01:31,648
Yeah.

13
00:01:31,648 --> 00:01:34,348
But, wow... I've never seen
anything like this.

14
00:01:34,348 --> 00:01:37,829
Wow, this is unbelievable.
A gun murder in South Korea?

15
00:01:37,829 --> 00:01:41,014
So I've been thinking,
could this possibly be...

16
00:01:41,014 --> 00:01:42,581
The victim's identity?

17
00:01:45,125 --> 00:01:46,648
Sir, here it is.

18
00:01:48,214 --> 00:01:50,881
Hwang Min Ho, 38 years old.

19
00:01:50,881 --> 00:01:52,531
The interesting thing is that
he was just released

20
00:01:52,531 --> 00:01:53,981
after serving time for murder.

21
00:01:53,981 --> 00:01:57,281
He staged his pregnant wife's death
and collected the insurance.

22
00:01:57,281 --> 00:01:59,481
He served three years
and got out three days ago.

23
00:01:59,481 --> 00:02:03,381
Just three years?
That's all he got for murder?

24
00:02:04,448 --> 00:02:05,914
It was ruled as a drunk driving case.

25
00:02:05,914 --> 00:02:08,548
His wife, who was
in the passenger seat, died.

26
00:02:08,548 --> 00:02:10,789
They could never prove
it was a planned accident,

27
00:02:10,789 --> 00:02:12,965
so he only got vehicular homicide.

28
00:02:12,965 --> 00:02:16,048
So, I've been thinking, could this be...

29
00:02:16,048 --> 00:02:18,014
Estimated time of death?

30
00:02:19,648 --> 00:02:23,514
According to the coroner, it appears that
at least 12 hours have passed.

31
00:02:23,514 --> 00:02:25,248
He had a 4 a.m. wake-up call request,

32
00:02:25,248 --> 00:02:27,014
but he didn't answer, so a staff member
went up and found him.

33
00:02:27,014 --> 00:02:29,614
He had a ticket to the Philippines,

34
00:02:29,614 --> 00:02:31,348
so he was probably planning
to catch the first flight out.

35
00:02:31,348 --> 00:02:34,914
Looks like he was taking the money
and running overseas to start a new life.

36
00:02:34,914 --> 00:02:36,448
12 hours?

37
00:02:37,348 --> 00:02:39,581
So that would've been yesterday afternoon?

38
00:02:52,214 --> 00:02:54,981
The window was still open
when the staff member arrived.

39
00:02:54,981 --> 00:02:57,114
Clearly a chain-smoker.

40
00:02:58,048 --> 00:03:01,514
Wow... Where on earth
did the bullet come from?

41
00:03:02,348 --> 00:03:04,814
Sir! I found this!

42
00:03:06,981 --> 00:03:08,948
It's a bullet!
Wow, a bullet is lodged in here.

43
00:03:08,948 --> 00:03:10,014
A real one-shot, one-kill...

44
00:03:10,014 --> 00:03:11,814
- Keep it down.
- Yes, sir.

45
00:03:55,548 --> 00:03:57,381
No, no way...

46
00:03:57,381 --> 00:04:01,381
Even so, that's way too far...

47
00:04:48,814 --> 00:04:51,314
What are you doing? What's going on?

48
00:04:51,314 --> 00:04:52,914
I know you're the police,

49
00:04:52,914 --> 00:04:54,881
but barging into
a sacred church this early...

50
00:04:54,881 --> 00:04:57,681
Sir, I know this must be a shock.
It was for me too.

51
00:04:57,681 --> 00:04:59,048
- Please don't be too alarmed.
- But...

52
00:04:59,048 --> 00:05:03,548
- First, about today's scripture reading...
- You need permission first!

53
00:05:24,148 --> 00:05:27,114
No way. Is that even possible from that far?

54
00:05:27,114 --> 00:05:28,448
Can you even see that?

55
00:05:28,448 --> 00:05:31,414
Oh, maybe the gun is just that good?
What kind of gun is it?

56
00:05:31,414 --> 00:05:33,414
Quit yapping.

57
00:05:33,414 --> 00:05:36,181
Hey, Beom, what is
the first thing we should do?

58
00:05:36,181 --> 00:05:39,214
Secure the CCTV footage first.

59
00:05:39,214 --> 00:05:40,514
Go check.

60
00:05:40,514 --> 00:05:42,757
If this is the sniper's position,

61
00:05:42,757 --> 00:05:45,548
we should at least
be able to narrow down the time.

62
00:05:46,181 --> 00:05:48,314
- Sorry?
- The time of the shooting.

63
00:05:48,314 --> 00:05:52,081
Not just the church's cameras.
Every CCTV nearby would've been wiped.

64
00:05:52,081 --> 00:05:56,148
The moment the footage disappears,
that's the time of the crime.

65
00:05:56,148 --> 00:05:58,581
How could you possibly...

66
00:05:58,581 --> 00:06:01,248
Didn't you say you secretly
looked into all this on your own?

67
00:06:04,714 --> 00:06:07,648
Then could this be... As I suspected...

68
00:06:12,914 --> 00:06:14,714
I think that punk is back.

69
00:06:14,714 --> 00:06:16,348
No way...

70
00:06:24,848 --> 00:06:28,381
Nice to see you again, Kingfisher.

71
00:06:29,414 --> 00:06:34,053
- Please take good care of my kid.
- Walk, please.

72
00:06:34,053 --> 00:06:36,881
- I'll see you later.
- Yeah.

73
00:06:37,614 --> 00:06:39,214
- I know a good cafe...
- Oh, it's Yul!

74
00:06:39,214 --> 00:06:41,181
Are you happy I'm taking you today?

75
00:06:41,181 --> 00:06:42,448
Yeah, I like it!

76
00:06:42,448 --> 00:06:43,581
Then I should come more often.

77
00:06:43,581 --> 00:06:45,957
Yeah, come every single day!

78
00:06:45,957 --> 00:06:47,497
Hello!

79
00:06:48,181 --> 00:06:51,248
- Good morning, Miss.
- Good morning.

80
00:06:51,248 --> 00:06:55,269
Good morning, Miss.
I'm Kwon Tae Seong, Yul's dad.

81
00:06:55,269 --> 00:06:57,481
- It's nice to meet you.
- Oh, hello.

82
00:06:57,481 --> 00:07:00,181
- Please take good care of Yul today.
- He says he's Yul's dad.

83
00:07:01,614 --> 00:07:04,881
Have fun today, Yul. See you tonight.

84
00:07:04,881 --> 00:07:06,514
You should do that with me.

85
00:07:06,514 --> 00:07:08,248
Do what?

86
00:07:08,248 --> 00:07:10,814
Oh, this is something Yul's mom
used to do for her every day.

87
00:07:10,814 --> 00:07:12,314
Let me show you.

88
00:07:12,314 --> 00:07:17,781
She goes, "My Yul, today, too,
with friends, get along well!"

89
00:07:17,781 --> 00:07:19,589
My Yul, today, too,

90
00:07:19,589 --> 00:07:21,701
- with friends, get along well!
- With friends, get along well!

91
00:07:21,701 --> 00:07:22,714
Say goodbye to your dad.

92
00:07:22,714 --> 00:07:25,314
- Bye-bye!
- Let's go inside, Yul. Be careful!

93
00:07:25,314 --> 00:07:26,681
Careful. Take it slow.

94
00:07:26,681 --> 00:07:28,514
Have a good day.

95
00:07:34,248 --> 00:07:37,948
So she had her husband's help.
That explains it.

96
00:07:37,948 --> 00:07:39,314
He's handsome.

97
00:07:39,314 --> 00:07:41,648
Yul's mom really has it all.

98
00:08:03,848 --> 00:08:07,781
Good morning! You're here again today.

99
00:08:12,614 --> 00:08:14,148
Good morning.

100
00:08:15,914 --> 00:08:18,248
Oh, Bong! Mr. Bong.

101
00:08:21,014 --> 00:08:23,081
Wow, Mr. Han!

102
00:08:23,813 --> 00:08:25,648
Oh, I didn't realize you were here.

103
00:08:25,648 --> 00:08:28,914
What a pleasant surprise
first thing in the morning.

104
00:08:28,914 --> 00:08:31,914
You're so pathetic
first thing in the morning.

105
00:08:31,914 --> 00:08:35,981
What is it this time? Lettuce?
Two bags of it?

106
00:08:37,881 --> 00:08:43,848
Oh, by the way, I heard that
Team 2 topped fan sales again.

107
00:08:43,848 --> 00:08:45,214
Congrats!

108
00:08:45,214 --> 00:08:47,514
You don't have to congratulate us
for doing what we always do.

109
00:08:47,514 --> 00:08:49,914
- Yeah, I know.
- I'm tired of hearing it.

110
00:08:49,914 --> 00:08:52,281
We also took first in dehumidifiers
and air purifiers.

111
00:08:54,714 --> 00:08:56,281
What about Team 3?

112
00:08:56,281 --> 00:09:01,781
Us? Same as always. Dead last every month.

113
00:09:01,781 --> 00:09:07,148
You're way too soft. That's your problem.

114
00:09:07,148 --> 00:09:10,148
Salespeople have to be
ruthless when it counts.

115
00:09:10,148 --> 00:09:11,648
Exactly.

116
00:09:14,414 --> 00:09:15,581
What are you doing? Get in!

117
00:09:15,581 --> 00:09:17,548
Oh, I gotta go.

118
00:09:22,681 --> 00:09:26,281
No wonder your whole team's
got no fight in them.

119
00:09:26,281 --> 00:09:27,814
That's right.

120
00:09:30,281 --> 00:09:31,481
Good morning!

121
00:09:31,481 --> 00:09:33,014
Come on in.

122
00:09:34,214 --> 00:09:36,181
Oh, my, hang on a second.

123
00:09:37,048 --> 00:09:38,514
Good morning.

124
00:09:38,514 --> 00:09:40,248
Keep up the good work.

125
00:09:43,948 --> 00:09:45,581
Director Yoo!

126
00:09:52,248 --> 00:09:54,314
Team Leader Han, have you been well?

127
00:09:54,314 --> 00:09:55,685
Oh, yeah, Director Yoo.

128
00:09:55,685 --> 00:09:57,381
- I heard you're back.
- Yeah.

129
00:09:57,381 --> 00:09:58,748
Enjoy your break?

130
00:09:58,748 --> 00:10:00,814
<i>Break, my foot.</i>

131
00:10:00,814 --> 00:10:02,981
Well, yeah.

132
00:10:02,981 --> 00:10:06,281
Others take a year or two off,
but you took a whole three years.

133
00:10:06,281 --> 00:10:09,614
Now that you're back,
you'd better make up for lost time.

134
00:10:09,614 --> 00:10:14,381
You're the ace of that team.
Time to make up for what you missed.

135
00:10:14,381 --> 00:10:16,048
Absolutely.

136
00:10:16,048 --> 00:10:17,281
I'll do my best.

137
00:10:17,281 --> 00:10:18,781
Good.

138
00:10:20,114 --> 00:10:22,248
Just get it together, seriously.

139
00:10:22,248 --> 00:10:23,301
How do you manage to rank last

140
00:10:23,301 --> 00:10:26,114
every month, quarter, year,
and product category?

141
00:10:26,114 --> 00:10:28,381
It's not like
you're some kind of killer group.

142
00:10:30,881 --> 00:10:33,114
What's the point of us
busting our asses downstairs

143
00:10:33,114 --> 00:10:36,648
when a team dragging down
the average gets to sit pretty upstairs?

144
00:10:38,448 --> 00:10:39,781
Go on up.

145
00:10:39,781 --> 00:10:42,681
- Enjoy your rabbit food.
- Yeah.

146
00:10:42,681 --> 00:10:44,214
Go.

147
00:10:48,381 --> 00:10:50,414
Shall I schedule a meeting?

148
00:10:55,234 --> 00:10:56,457
[Not Today]

149
00:10:56,481 --> 00:10:59,181
- Good morning!
- Good morning.

150
00:10:59,181 --> 00:11:00,714
- Good morning.
- Morning.

151
00:11:03,248 --> 00:11:05,573
Hello.

152
00:11:06,414 --> 00:11:07,448
What?

153
00:11:07,448 --> 00:11:08,514
I heard you got a big one?

154
00:11:08,514 --> 00:11:10,501
- It's nothing new, right?
- Right.

155
00:11:24,848 --> 00:11:31,581
"Musan Car Explosion Victim Identified As
10-time Convicted Drug Kingpin."

156
00:11:32,214 --> 00:11:35,148
Wow, now that's a sexy headline.

157
00:11:35,148 --> 00:11:37,414
Explosion, drugs.

158
00:11:38,181 --> 00:11:40,714
Be honest with me, okay?

159
00:11:40,714 --> 00:11:42,148
You just got lucky with this one, right?

160
00:11:42,148 --> 00:11:43,848
Yeah.

161
00:11:43,848 --> 00:11:47,048
Really? You really just got lucky?
By coincidence?

162
00:11:47,914 --> 00:11:49,914
Bae Doo Hyuk...

163
00:11:50,548 --> 00:11:54,181
He worked with an international drug ring
to manufacture and distribute drugs.

164
00:11:54,181 --> 00:11:58,514
A former gangster with ten prior convictions
for murder solicitation and violence.

165
00:11:58,514 --> 00:12:01,448
And this guy just happened to,
on the exact day you went to Musan...

166
00:12:01,448 --> 00:12:03,749
His last crime was aggravated assault,

167
00:12:03,749 --> 00:12:06,581
for which he got three years,
and he was released two months ago.

168
00:12:06,581 --> 00:12:09,048
The moment he got out, he went down
to Musan and started causing trouble...

169
00:12:09,048 --> 00:12:12,048
And after running wild like that,
on the very day you went to Musan...

170
00:12:12,048 --> 00:12:13,981
- Bang!
- Wow, you scared me.

171
00:12:13,981 --> 00:12:16,781
- He's dead.
- What's this?

172
00:12:16,781 --> 00:12:17,981
What on earth is this?

173
00:12:17,981 --> 00:12:20,848
Do you really think
this was just an accident?

174
00:12:20,848 --> 00:12:23,648
Or is it more likely someone killed him
and staged it as an accident?

175
00:12:23,648 --> 00:12:28,048
Hey, you went after the drug kingpin
yourself all the way there?

176
00:12:28,048 --> 00:12:31,381
You're insane. You still haven't
come to your senses.

177
00:12:31,381 --> 00:12:33,848
You did the same thing years ago, remember?
You almost got yourself killed.

178
00:12:33,848 --> 00:12:35,914
That... What was it? Kingfisher.

179
00:12:35,914 --> 00:12:39,981
You almost got killed
by Kingfisher's bullet. Ah, really.

180
00:12:41,821 --> 00:12:42,821
- <i>Breaking news.</i>
- What is it?

181
00:12:42,821 --> 00:12:45,714
- <i>A shooting using a sniper rifle</i>
- What's that?

182
00:12:45,714 --> 00:12:47,881
<i>has occurred in the heart of Seoul.</i>

183
00:12:47,881 --> 00:12:50,581
- <i>Some speculate that Kingfisher,</i>
- Speak of the devil, is that it?

184
00:12:50,581 --> 00:12:54,948
<i>the infamous serial gun killer
who disappeared for the past four years,</i>

185
00:12:54,948 --> 00:12:57,181
- <i>may have returned.</i>
- Turn it up.

186
00:12:57,181 --> 00:13:00,614
<i>The incident took place at a hotel
in Jeonjak-dong, Seoul.</i>

187
00:13:00,614 --> 00:13:01,848
[Breaking News: Kingfisher Returns?]
<i>A man in his thirties,</i>

188
00:13:01,848 --> 00:13:02,848
[Shooting Homicide in Seoul]
<i>identified as Mr. Hwang,</i>

189
00:13:02,848 --> 00:13:07,448
<i>was struck and killed by a bullet
fired from outside the building.</i>

190
00:13:07,448 --> 00:13:10,581
<i>For more details, we'll soon connect live to
our reporter on the scene</i>

191
00:13:10,581 --> 00:13:14,548
<i>for the latest on the police investigation.</i>

192
00:13:15,681 --> 00:13:18,648
<i>The incident took place at a hotel
in Jeonjak-dong, Seoul.</i>

193
00:13:18,648 --> 00:13:21,181
<i>A man in his thirties,
identified as Mr. Hwang,</i>

194
00:13:21,181 --> 00:13:25,014
<i>was struck and killed by a bullet
fired from outside the building.</i>

195
00:13:25,014 --> 00:13:27,081
[Jeonjak-dong Hotel]
<i>Considering the use of a sniper rifle</i>

196
00:13:27,081 --> 00:13:28,709
[Kingfisher Sniper Incident]
<i>and the victim's criminal history,</i>

197
00:13:28,709 --> 00:13:30,881
<i>police see this as the first such case</i>

198
00:13:30,881 --> 00:13:32,714
<i>since the Haegong-dong
boarding house case four years ago...</i>

199
00:13:32,714 --> 00:13:34,014
Mom, thanks for the meal.

200
00:13:34,014 --> 00:13:36,381
Okay, hurry along.

201
00:13:36,381 --> 00:13:37,477
<i>Some speculate that Kingfisher,</i>

202
00:13:37,477 --> 00:13:38,981
- <i>the infamous serial gun killer...</i>
- Sun Il, look at that.

203
00:13:38,981 --> 00:13:41,514
<i>They are keeping a close eye
on the situation.</i>

204
00:13:41,514 --> 00:13:43,414
Tae Seong is going to be busy again.

205
00:13:43,414 --> 00:13:46,681
<i>Kingfisher is the nickname
for a professional sniper killer</i>

206
00:13:46,681 --> 00:13:48,677
<i>who has killed 93 people to date,</i>

207
00:13:48,677 --> 00:13:51,081
<i>starting with the 2010 Semyung-dong shooting.</i>

208
00:13:51,081 --> 00:13:52,645
- <i>Despite committing serious crimes,</i>
- Kwon Tae Seong!

209
00:13:52,645 --> 00:13:53,645
<i>criminals just received light sentences</i>

210
00:13:53,645 --> 00:13:54,645
- <i>and were released.</i>
- Come in here.

211
00:13:54,645 --> 00:13:56,293
<i>The killings are characterized</i>

212
00:13:56,293 --> 00:13:59,214
<i>by targeting criminals
with high recidivism rates.</i>

213
00:13:59,214 --> 00:14:01,893
<i>If this incident is confirmed
to be the work of Kingfisher,</i>

214
00:14:01,893 --> 00:14:04,293
<i>it would mean that the infamous serial killer</i>

215
00:14:04,293 --> 00:14:07,648
<i>who once shook the nation
has returned after four years,</i>

216
00:14:07,648 --> 00:14:11,948
<i>causing another major shock
and public concern.</i>

217
00:14:11,948 --> 00:14:16,281
Why would you hand that
over to someone else? Why?

218
00:14:16,281 --> 00:14:19,448
It's not about why. You know
I'm already covering another case.

219
00:14:19,448 --> 00:14:21,214
What? The drug kingpin case?

220
00:14:21,214 --> 00:14:23,581
You think drugs matter right now?

221
00:14:23,581 --> 00:14:26,848
When just the name 'Kingfisher'
triples the viewership?

222
00:14:26,848 --> 00:14:28,869
Besides, you're the reporter
covering Kingfisher.

223
00:14:28,869 --> 00:14:31,081
Who else would you give it to?

224
00:14:31,081 --> 00:14:34,214
Come on, that was ages ago...

225
00:14:34,214 --> 00:14:35,581
What happened to you?

226
00:14:35,581 --> 00:14:38,548
You used to run out of the room
the second you heard the name Kingfisher.

227
00:14:38,548 --> 00:14:42,948
And now, after all these years,
I'm in charge of investigative reporting...

228
00:14:42,948 --> 00:14:45,448
Exactly. Investigative reporting.

229
00:14:45,448 --> 00:14:47,914
So what is the one thing
people are most curious about right now?

230
00:14:47,914 --> 00:14:52,048
Isn't it why Kingfisher disappeared
for four years and came back alive?

231
00:14:52,048 --> 00:14:54,614
So you can dig deep into that!

232
00:14:55,281 --> 00:14:57,548
Chief, that Bae Doo Hyuk

233
00:14:57,548 --> 00:15:00,748
was a major figure who controlled
half of Korea's drug supply and distribution.

234
00:15:00,748 --> 00:15:04,014
There's a high chance this wasn't
an accident but a murder.

235
00:15:04,014 --> 00:15:06,081
Then who do you think is behind it?

236
00:15:06,081 --> 00:15:10,848
That's exactly what I want to investigate.
I'll really give it my all this time.

237
00:15:10,848 --> 00:15:14,714
So you keep fighting too, Chief.

238
00:15:15,348 --> 00:15:16,714
I'll get going.

239
00:15:16,714 --> 00:15:17,948
Hey! Tae Seong!

240
00:15:17,948 --> 00:15:19,614
Hey, Kwon Tae Seong!

241
00:15:20,981 --> 00:15:24,414
Did he eat something weird?
What's gotten into him?

242
00:15:29,351 --> 00:15:30,834
[Reporter Kwon Tae Seong]

243
00:15:31,581 --> 00:15:35,381
How badly did you handle the scene
for the news to leak already?

244
00:15:36,414 --> 00:15:40,448
A shooting happened in South Korea.
You really think we can cover it up?

245
00:15:40,448 --> 00:15:42,148
Are you sure it's Kingfisher?

246
00:15:42,148 --> 00:15:45,048
It could be someone else.
It could be a copycat crime, for instance.

247
00:15:45,048 --> 00:15:46,081
Who would do that?

248
00:15:46,081 --> 00:15:48,381
It's not just any gun.
A sniper shot from 500 meters away?

249
00:15:48,381 --> 00:15:50,381
I mean, besides that guy...

250
00:15:50,381 --> 00:15:53,681
That punk was quiet for four years.

251
00:15:53,681 --> 00:15:57,748
Why now, all of a sudden?
And why our district of all places?

252
00:15:57,748 --> 00:15:59,181
No need for a long explanation.

253
00:15:59,181 --> 00:16:01,314
Can you catch him or not?

254
00:16:01,314 --> 00:16:02,848
We'll investigate.

255
00:16:02,848 --> 00:16:04,881
Good. If you're going to catch him,
do it quickly.

256
00:16:04,881 --> 00:16:07,481
If it looks impossible,
wrap it up quietly when the time is right.

257
00:16:07,481 --> 00:16:09,848
Don't make a big scene for no reason.

258
00:16:09,848 --> 00:16:13,181
The higher-ups aren't expecting much anyway.

259
00:16:13,181 --> 00:16:16,648
People considered the best of the best
couldn't catch him for 16 years in 93 tries.

260
00:16:16,648 --> 00:16:18,948
What makes us any different?

261
00:16:19,981 --> 00:16:25,448
Even you, the ace of Violent Crimes,
couldn't catch him once.

262
00:16:30,314 --> 00:16:34,781
If we just drag our feet, he'll probably
move on somewhere else soon.

263
00:16:34,781 --> 00:16:36,414
Just until then...

264
00:16:37,748 --> 00:16:39,414
Hey, I'm talking to you.

265
00:16:39,414 --> 00:16:42,981
Hey, you handle the briefing too.
Just wing it.

266
00:16:49,147 --> 00:16:50,890
[Violent Crimes Team 1]

267
00:16:50,914 --> 00:16:52,981
- You're here.
- Yeah.

268
00:16:58,814 --> 00:17:00,314
What are you doing?

269
00:17:01,714 --> 00:17:05,481
I was curious why he's called Kingfisher,
so I looked it up.

270
00:17:05,481 --> 00:17:08,448
Wow, it just means "kingfisher" in Korean.

271
00:17:08,448 --> 00:17:10,814
I seriously thought it was the kind of bird
that shoots water guns or something.

272
00:17:10,814 --> 00:17:15,381
But apparently, its beak is long
and shaped almost like a sniper rifle.

273
00:17:15,381 --> 00:17:16,773
It perches way up high.

274
00:17:16,773 --> 00:17:20,514
The moment it spots prey,
it shoots into the water like a bullet...

275
00:17:20,514 --> 00:17:22,181
Are you out of your mind?

276
00:17:22,181 --> 00:17:24,648
Is this really the time for you
to be wasting time on this nonsense?

277
00:17:27,748 --> 00:17:32,181
I checked the CCTV center.
Just as we thought, all footage was erased.

278
00:17:32,181 --> 00:17:35,148
The witnesses inside the church
were in choir practice at the time,

279
00:17:35,148 --> 00:17:37,381
so they were all gathered in the main hall
and didn't see anything.

280
00:17:37,381 --> 00:17:41,114
The singing was so loud
that they didn't hear anything either.

281
00:17:41,114 --> 00:17:42,481
Choir?

282
00:17:42,481 --> 00:17:44,848
What about the people who drove,
the ones with dashcams?

283
00:17:44,848 --> 00:17:46,814
I already asked about that.

284
00:17:46,814 --> 00:17:49,448
There were seven people
who drove to the church that day.

285
00:17:49,448 --> 00:17:51,973
But the above-ground parking lot
was closed off,

286
00:17:51,973 --> 00:17:53,848
so they all parked underground.

287
00:17:53,848 --> 00:17:58,848
But the church says they never
blocked the above-ground parking lot.

288
00:17:58,848 --> 00:18:03,014
Of course, they didn't.
Someone else must have.

289
00:18:03,014 --> 00:18:04,414
Yeah, someone else...

290
00:18:04,414 --> 00:18:07,314
What? What do you mean, someone else?

291
00:18:10,214 --> 00:18:11,714
- Come with me.
- What?

292
00:18:12,414 --> 00:18:16,214
Study all the Kingfisher
case files by tomorrow.

293
00:18:16,214 --> 00:18:18,148
Memorize every single detail.

294
00:18:19,481 --> 00:18:21,381
Got it?

295
00:18:21,381 --> 00:18:23,181
Wait, all this in one day?

296
00:18:23,181 --> 00:18:25,081
This isn't even cramming for an exam.

297
00:18:25,081 --> 00:18:26,181
I'll test you.

298
00:18:26,181 --> 00:18:27,748
Yes, sir!

299
00:18:27,748 --> 00:18:29,348
Good luck.

300
00:18:33,548 --> 00:18:35,742
[The Kingfisher Case Files]

301
00:18:37,614 --> 00:18:40,648
When did he even collect all of this?

302
00:18:40,648 --> 00:18:41,733
[About Kingfisher,]
<i>Sniper attacks</i>

303
00:18:41,733 --> 00:18:43,781
[are we not catching him,]
<i>are one of the most difficult crimes</i>

304
00:18:43,781 --> 00:18:46,214
[or can we not catch him?]
<i>to investigate and solve.</i>

305
00:18:46,214 --> 00:18:49,157
<i>There are usually no clues
left behind at the crime scene,</i>

306
00:18:49,157 --> 00:18:51,514
<i>such as fingerprints, footprints, or DNA.</i>

307
00:18:51,514 --> 00:18:55,981
<i>It's also extremely difficult to determine
where the shot was fired from.</i>

308
00:18:55,981 --> 00:18:58,014
<i>And even if we take the time to find it,</i>

309
00:18:58,014 --> 00:19:01,148
<i>any traces that may have been
left at the sniper's position</i>

310
00:19:01,148 --> 00:19:02,648
<i>will already be gone.</i>

311
00:19:02,648 --> 00:19:04,981
It's been a long time
since I've seen this on the news.

312
00:19:04,981 --> 00:19:07,948
It'll probably be all over the news for days.

313
00:19:07,948 --> 00:19:11,214
By the way, everything's okay, right?

314
00:19:12,114 --> 00:19:15,148
You know what Bo Na's like. Don't worry.

315
00:19:15,148 --> 00:19:19,614
Well, I'm not worried or anything,
but... why was her leg shaking?

316
00:19:21,281 --> 00:19:22,781
What about you, Team Leader?

317
00:19:22,781 --> 00:19:27,381
Hey, my leg wasn't shaking.
It just cramped up for a second.

318
00:19:31,548 --> 00:19:36,014
Fine. Honestly, as the team leader,
I was a little concerned.

319
00:19:36,014 --> 00:19:38,581
It's been four years
since Director Yoo had her baby.

320
00:19:38,581 --> 00:19:43,148
Even athletes worry that they won't be
the same after taking just a year off.

321
00:19:43,148 --> 00:19:49,081
I wondered if she might be getting tired
or feeling nervous...

322
00:19:49,081 --> 00:19:52,148
What if she made a mistake?

323
00:19:52,148 --> 00:19:53,981
She said it gave her chills.

324
00:19:55,948 --> 00:19:57,614
Chills?

325
00:19:57,614 --> 00:19:59,014
It was creepy too.

326
00:19:59,014 --> 00:20:00,981
The great Yoo Bo Na?

327
00:20:05,081 --> 00:20:09,648
Wow, this place really hasn't changed.

328
00:20:09,648 --> 00:20:12,848
How do you even breathe, eat, and sleep here?

329
00:20:12,848 --> 00:20:16,181
When was your last health checkup?
Do you ever even go home?

330
00:20:16,181 --> 00:20:19,848
You're here? That was quite a greeting.

331
00:20:19,848 --> 00:20:23,848
Pulled another all-nighter, huh?
What were you tinkering with all night?

332
00:20:23,848 --> 00:20:28,814
The boss wanted me to make something
flow smoothly, like this and that.

333
00:20:28,814 --> 00:20:33,214
So I made it, but I was looking for
one more source.

334
00:20:33,214 --> 00:20:34,648
Oh, really?

335
00:20:34,648 --> 00:20:37,348
So I played around with it
like this and that.

336
00:20:37,348 --> 00:20:40,314
And turns out it's a flying fly.
The fly just kind of...

337
00:20:48,348 --> 00:20:50,014
You changed your gear a bit?

338
00:20:50,014 --> 00:20:54,514
Oh, you noticed? That's Yoo Bo Na for you.

339
00:20:57,381 --> 00:21:02,148
It's a bit lighter and has less vibration.

340
00:21:02,148 --> 00:21:05,014
The ammunition must have changed too.

341
00:21:05,014 --> 00:21:07,348
It's fine. It only took a few months.

342
00:21:07,348 --> 00:21:09,814
- Do you like it?
- Yeah.

343
00:21:09,814 --> 00:21:11,248
Thanks to you, it was much better.

344
00:21:11,248 --> 00:21:15,381
My kid has grown so much lately.
She's 16 kilograms now.

345
00:21:15,381 --> 00:21:17,381
My gift for your comeback.

346
00:21:30,081 --> 00:21:35,014
Yes, Miss! What? What is it?

347
00:21:35,014 --> 00:21:36,548
What?

348
00:21:45,348 --> 00:21:48,814
Wait, you mean what made Director Yoo nervous
was because of her child?

349
00:21:50,248 --> 00:21:53,781
Yul sleeps well, and this morning...

350
00:21:53,781 --> 00:21:57,848
Was Director Yoo in there?
Without even wearing a mask?

351
00:21:57,848 --> 00:22:00,748
Could you let me video call her?
I'll try talking to her.

352
00:22:00,748 --> 00:22:02,914
Yeah, I'll set it up.

353
00:22:04,948 --> 00:22:06,514
Yul!

354
00:22:07,281 --> 00:22:11,581
Oh, my Yul! Why don't you want to take a nap?

355
00:22:11,581 --> 00:22:13,881
All your friends are sleeping. Why don't you?

356
00:22:13,881 --> 00:22:16,881
A monster appeared in my dream,
and I'm scared.

357
00:22:16,881 --> 00:22:21,914
Oh, a monster appeared in your dream?
Is that what happened?

358
00:22:21,914 --> 00:22:26,014
Should I sing your favorite Baby Shark's
My Dream Is a Superhero?

359
00:22:26,014 --> 00:22:29,148
You know all the monsters run away
when we sing that song, right?

360
00:22:29,148 --> 00:22:30,381
Alright, good!

361
00:22:30,381 --> 00:22:32,448
<i>Okay, I'm starting! Here we go.</i>

362
00:22:32,448 --> 00:22:35,348
<i>♪ I'm going to be a superhero ♪</i>

363
00:22:35,348 --> 00:22:38,048
<i>♪ I will save the whole wide world ♪</i>

364
00:22:38,048 --> 00:22:40,181
<i>♪ Bang, bang, bang ♪</i>

365
00:22:40,181 --> 00:22:43,173
<i>♪ My dream is to be a superhero ♪</i>

366
00:22:43,173 --> 00:22:44,973
How is it?

367
00:22:46,948 --> 00:22:50,048
- That gives me chills. It's creepy too.
- You like it?

368
00:22:50,048 --> 00:22:52,781
So, the great Kingfisher has become a mom?

369
00:22:52,781 --> 00:22:56,517
It's unfamiliar. It's very unfamiliar.

370
00:22:56,517 --> 00:22:59,281
<i>♪ I'm going to be a superhero ♪</i>

371
00:22:59,281 --> 00:23:02,048
<i>♪ I will save the whole wide world ♪</i>

372
00:23:02,048 --> 00:23:04,881
<i>♪ Bang, bang, bang ♪</i>

373
00:23:04,881 --> 00:23:08,481
<i>♪ My dream is to be a superhero ♪</i>

374
00:23:15,814 --> 00:23:18,981
Detective Lee Dong Jin, you're here.

375
00:23:18,981 --> 00:23:22,281
You must be working around the clock
with such a major case

376
00:23:22,281 --> 00:23:24,148
happening in your district.

377
00:23:24,148 --> 00:23:26,348
Please have a seat over here.

378
00:23:26,348 --> 00:23:29,314
Reporter Kwon Tae Seong, it's been a while.

379
00:23:29,314 --> 00:23:32,081
You only come looking for me
when something like this happens.

380
00:23:32,081 --> 00:23:33,781
Sorry.

381
00:23:34,781 --> 00:23:36,514
Hey, you're paying today.

382
00:23:36,514 --> 00:23:38,914
Come on, people are watching. Sit down.

383
00:23:38,914 --> 00:23:41,581
I already ordered. The most expensive one.

384
00:23:46,281 --> 00:23:47,881
Looks expensive.

385
00:23:48,514 --> 00:23:49,748
- Enjoy your meal.
- Yeah.

386
00:23:49,748 --> 00:23:51,414
Thank you.

387
00:23:53,948 --> 00:23:57,781
Just get to the point.
I have to head back right after I eat.

388
00:23:57,781 --> 00:24:00,914
You always act like you're busy.
I'm busy too.

389
00:24:01,781 --> 00:24:05,414
You're covering the Kingfisher story, right?
That's why you're here.

390
00:24:05,414 --> 00:24:08,914
The juniors handle that stuff now.
I've moved on.

391
00:24:08,914 --> 00:24:11,914
You saw the news.
It's exactly what it looks like.

392
00:24:11,914 --> 00:24:14,248
Nothing more to tell you.

393
00:24:17,748 --> 00:24:22,748
- No need to get you anything expensive.
- Hey, that's mine. Eat yours.

394
00:24:27,481 --> 00:24:29,281
Is it really the Kingfisher?

395
00:24:30,948 --> 00:24:35,414
Oh, my, why does everyone ask me that
the moment they see me?

396
00:24:36,548 --> 00:24:38,781
If I answer, will you write it?

397
00:24:38,781 --> 00:24:41,248
I told you I wouldn't.

398
00:24:41,948 --> 00:24:43,648
- You won't?
- I won't.

399
00:24:43,648 --> 00:24:45,248
Why not?

400
00:24:45,248 --> 00:24:47,381
You're the Kingfisher expert.

401
00:24:47,381 --> 00:24:50,081
Now that I think about it,
four years ago in Haegong-dong too...

402
00:24:50,081 --> 00:24:51,714
Is it Kingfisher?

403
00:25:02,714 --> 00:25:06,381
Well, the method
and victim profiles are similar,

404
00:25:06,381 --> 00:25:08,648
but it's still just speculation.

405
00:25:09,514 --> 00:25:11,914
The weapon is different,

406
00:25:11,914 --> 00:25:14,848
and the fact that he rarely carried out
daytime shootings bothers me.

407
00:25:14,848 --> 00:25:18,548
No, forget the official theory.
What's your gut telling you?

408
00:25:23,148 --> 00:25:26,581
One hundred percent Kingfisher.

409
00:25:30,514 --> 00:25:33,114
I thought he retired four years ago.

410
00:25:33,114 --> 00:25:36,281
Hey, what retirement does a killer have?

411
00:25:38,048 --> 00:25:42,448
What are the differences between
the case four years ago and this one?

412
00:25:42,448 --> 00:25:45,781
You were at both scenes, so you'd know.
Anything, even a small detail.

413
00:25:45,781 --> 00:25:48,348
Like, you found anything
at the shooting site...

414
00:25:49,414 --> 00:25:51,348
You're unbelievable.
Did you come here knowing something?

415
00:25:51,348 --> 00:25:53,581
You found something? What is it?

416
00:25:57,814 --> 00:25:59,314
<i>Baby Shark.</i>

417
00:25:59,314 --> 00:26:01,148
What?

418
00:26:01,148 --> 00:26:02,648
A sticker.

419
00:26:06,348 --> 00:26:08,381
What, a sticker?

420
00:26:08,381 --> 00:26:09,914
Yeah.

421
00:26:11,814 --> 00:26:16,181
I sent it to the NFS just in case,
but they said there were no fingerprints,

422
00:26:16,181 --> 00:26:20,314
and that it was something you could
easily buy at most stores or online.

423
00:26:20,314 --> 00:26:23,748
Which means every household in Korea
with kids probably has one.

424
00:26:23,748 --> 00:26:26,081
Dozens of Baby Sharks.

425
00:26:26,081 --> 00:26:29,881
The sharks in our house even have babies.

426
00:26:32,681 --> 00:26:35,481
Looks like Kingfisher
is a Baby Shark fanatic just like my Yul.

427
00:26:35,481 --> 00:26:38,814
Hey, this would blow up the views
if I wrote about it.

428
00:26:46,181 --> 00:26:48,048
This is good.

429
00:26:48,048 --> 00:26:50,614
Yul, what did you play with Chae Won today?

430
00:26:50,614 --> 00:26:52,948
[Baby Shark]
We played with this sticker.

431
00:26:52,948 --> 00:26:54,314
It's a Baby Shark sticker!

432
00:26:54,314 --> 00:26:56,114
Should I stick one on you too? This one?

433
00:26:56,114 --> 00:26:57,981
Should I put one on? Where should I put it?

434
00:26:57,981 --> 00:27:01,448
Mommy is the mommy shark.

435
00:27:01,448 --> 00:27:03,648
Mommy shark?

436
00:27:03,648 --> 00:27:06,514
This makes my clothes look even prettier.

437
00:27:06,514 --> 00:27:08,948
So what did you put on today?

438
00:27:08,948 --> 00:27:10,881
- Baby Shark.
- You put on a Baby Shark?

439
00:27:10,881 --> 00:27:13,881
This one is cute too. It looks like you.

440
00:27:13,881 --> 00:27:14,948
Yul!

441
00:27:14,948 --> 00:27:17,114
Daddy!

442
00:27:18,181 --> 00:27:20,314
My little precious!

443
00:27:20,314 --> 00:27:22,448
Come here, my big precious.

444
00:27:26,581 --> 00:27:29,848
Honey, why are you home so early?
Aren't you busy?

445
00:27:29,848 --> 00:27:32,381
I am busy. But today,
in the middle of all that,

446
00:27:32,381 --> 00:27:35,981
I had a sudden realization
that I missed my wife so much!

447
00:27:35,981 --> 00:27:37,748
What could I do then?
I had to run right over.

448
00:27:37,748 --> 00:27:42,281
Really? Why did you miss me so much today?

449
00:27:44,548 --> 00:27:45,748
You did something wrong, right?

450
00:27:45,748 --> 00:27:49,014
What would I have done wrong?
It's not like that, really.

451
00:27:49,014 --> 00:27:52,181
I really just wanted to see you,
so I came. Seriously.

452
00:27:52,181 --> 00:27:56,714
Then we must be connected by telepathy.
I really missed you today too.

453
00:27:56,714 --> 00:27:57,781
Really?

454
00:27:57,781 --> 00:27:59,281
Yeah.

455
00:28:07,381 --> 00:28:11,314
What is it?
Something happened today, didn't it?

456
00:28:11,314 --> 00:28:14,948
What do you mean? I'm just tired
from the business trip yesterday.

457
00:28:14,948 --> 00:28:17,014
Since we're already out,
should we grab dinner before going home?

458
00:28:17,014 --> 00:28:18,948
Yeah! Chicken! Chicken!

459
00:28:18,948 --> 00:28:21,348
Yul, do you want chicken?

460
00:28:21,348 --> 00:28:22,914
Should we go to Grandma's and eat chicken?

461
00:28:22,914 --> 00:28:25,581
Grandma's chicken is the best!

462
00:28:25,581 --> 00:28:27,114
Let's go.

463
00:28:27,114 --> 00:28:30,014
Let's go eat chicken.

464
00:28:37,448 --> 00:28:38,514
Enjoy your meal!

465
00:28:38,514 --> 00:28:40,614
- Let me know if you need anything.
- Grandma, Auntie!

466
00:28:40,614 --> 00:28:42,714
Pretty Yul is here.

467
00:28:42,714 --> 00:28:44,248
What brings you here at this hour?

468
00:28:44,248 --> 00:28:46,373
Oh, my, our pretty Yul is here?

469
00:28:46,373 --> 00:28:48,514
My son is here!

470
00:28:48,514 --> 00:28:50,581
Hey, come out here for a sec.

471
00:28:50,581 --> 00:28:53,081
Why is it so hard to see you these days?

472
00:28:53,081 --> 00:28:56,414
Oh, my, my little Yul!

473
00:28:58,914 --> 00:29:01,581
Yul, say hello to Grandma.
Give her a big greeting.

474
00:29:01,581 --> 00:29:03,414
Hello, Grandma.

475
00:29:03,414 --> 00:29:05,648
Good girl!

476
00:29:05,648 --> 00:29:09,048
But what brings you here?
Did you come straight from work?

477
00:29:09,048 --> 00:29:12,181
We ran into each other near home,
and Yul said she wanted chicken.

478
00:29:12,181 --> 00:29:14,248
Oh, did you?

479
00:29:14,248 --> 00:29:16,581
- Then come sit down. Sit down.
- Sit down.

480
00:29:17,214 --> 00:29:20,948
I will fry up
the most delicious chicken for my Yul!

481
00:29:20,948 --> 00:29:22,481
Okay.

482
00:29:24,014 --> 00:29:26,748
Since you're here anyway, stay and eat.

483
00:29:26,748 --> 00:29:30,314
But it's not good for children or adults
to eat takeout food too often.

484
00:29:30,314 --> 00:29:34,581
People who work outside all day
should come home to a warm homemade meal.

485
00:29:34,581 --> 00:29:36,581
It was me who wanted it.

486
00:29:36,581 --> 00:29:38,714
Okay, Mother.

487
00:29:40,614 --> 00:29:42,114
I was the one who asked...

488
00:29:43,248 --> 00:29:44,281
Welcome!

489
00:29:44,281 --> 00:29:47,581
- Sun Il, I should've done that. Sorry.
- Oh, please, sit down.

490
00:29:47,581 --> 00:29:49,981
Hey, hold it in today.

491
00:29:49,981 --> 00:29:52,481
Mom's finally in a good mood
after a while. Don't ruin it.

492
00:29:52,481 --> 00:29:55,914
Why? Why is Mom in a good mood?

493
00:29:55,914 --> 00:29:59,314
The landlord said
they'd freeze the rent again.

494
00:29:59,314 --> 00:30:03,648
Other shops raise their rent every year,
but ours hasn't changed for years.

495
00:30:03,648 --> 00:30:06,414
She was bragging about it to everyone.

496
00:30:06,414 --> 00:30:09,448
That's really kind of the landlord.
It's not easy to do that these days.

497
00:30:09,448 --> 00:30:11,481
Such an angel.

498
00:30:11,481 --> 00:30:13,481
We're busy right now, so wait just a little.

499
00:30:13,481 --> 00:30:14,948
Wait just a moment, Yul.

500
00:30:14,948 --> 00:30:16,481
Okay.

501
00:30:17,381 --> 00:30:20,048
I'm back!

502
00:30:20,048 --> 00:30:21,914
Bo Na, you're here?

503
00:30:21,914 --> 00:30:22,981
Auntie!

504
00:30:22,981 --> 00:30:26,414
Oh, my! Our cute Yul is here?

505
00:30:26,414 --> 00:30:28,281
Did you just finish a delivery?

506
00:30:28,281 --> 00:30:30,341
Yeah. Is it some special day?

507
00:30:30,341 --> 00:30:33,181
We got a bunch of
delivery orders all at once.

508
00:30:33,181 --> 00:30:34,514
You said you'd drink water, so drink up.

509
00:30:34,514 --> 00:30:37,648
By the way, why are you here
at this hour? Aren't you busy?

510
00:30:37,648 --> 00:30:39,048
I heard Kingfisher showed up.

511
00:30:39,048 --> 00:30:40,965
That was ages ago.
That's not my thing anymore.

512
00:30:40,965 --> 00:30:43,514
What about you? So, how have you been?

513
00:30:43,514 --> 00:30:45,748
Seriously, what have you been
hearing all this time?

514
00:30:45,748 --> 00:30:47,414
Same old, same old.

515
00:30:47,414 --> 00:30:51,381
I mean, I do have a social position
as a graduate student.

516
00:30:51,381 --> 00:30:54,948
But to Mom, that's the same
as being an unemployed bum.

517
00:30:54,948 --> 00:30:56,381
- Ah, seriously...
- That's why

518
00:30:56,381 --> 00:30:58,148
I keep telling you to hire part-timers.

519
00:30:58,148 --> 00:31:00,933
How can we afford
to hire people and pay them?

520
00:31:00,933 --> 00:31:02,714
Family members have to work hard together.

521
00:31:02,714 --> 00:31:07,314
You exploit your daughter for cheap labor.
You're a terrible employer!

522
00:31:07,314 --> 00:31:09,114
A terrible employer.

523
00:31:09,114 --> 00:31:10,914
All you do is talk.

524
00:31:10,914 --> 00:31:12,448
You know your sister-in-law
went back to work, right?

525
00:31:12,448 --> 00:31:15,214
- Yeah.
- If you look after Yul sometimes,

526
00:31:15,214 --> 00:31:20,381
I might, you know, increase your allowance.

527
00:31:20,381 --> 00:31:21,848
Really?

528
00:31:21,848 --> 00:31:26,714
Of course, I'd do anything for our Yul
even without allowance!

529
00:31:26,714 --> 00:31:30,181
But if you offer, I'll gladly accept.

530
00:31:31,081 --> 00:31:34,448
- I'll chip in too. Please help us.
- Done!

531
00:31:34,448 --> 00:31:36,881
Bo Na, how is it being back
at work? Do you like it?

532
00:31:36,881 --> 00:31:39,548
Oh, there's no way it could be good.
Is the work manageable?

533
00:31:39,548 --> 00:31:40,814
[Tae Seong Chicken]
Oh, dear.

534
00:31:40,814 --> 00:31:42,948
Why are you sitting in the customer's seat?
Hurry and go deliver.

535
00:31:42,948 --> 00:31:44,981
How is he a customer?

536
00:31:44,981 --> 00:31:46,514
The deliveries are piling up.

537
00:31:46,514 --> 00:31:48,114
Then at least pay me more.

538
00:31:48,114 --> 00:31:49,648
I'll be back.

539
00:31:53,914 --> 00:31:56,881
Did he go to prison for another crime?

540
00:31:56,881 --> 00:31:59,381
Was he seriously injured or sick?

541
00:32:00,101 --> 00:32:03,814
A vacation... A leave of absence?

542
00:32:03,814 --> 00:32:05,414
You've been saying that since earlier.

543
00:32:05,414 --> 00:32:09,681
What? Is being a murderer a job?
Retirement, leave of absence, vacation?

544
00:32:13,848 --> 00:32:18,714
He could've gotten married,
started a family, and had kids, like me.

545
00:32:18,714 --> 00:32:21,214
Even Kingfisher
could get married, unlike you...

546
00:32:21,914 --> 00:32:23,914
Watch what you say.
There's a gun at the station.

547
00:32:23,914 --> 00:32:25,548
Hey, that's disgusting! Hey!

548
00:32:25,548 --> 00:32:27,365
That's why you should get married, idiot.

549
00:32:27,365 --> 00:32:29,848
Stop living alone like some pathetic loser.

550
00:32:31,461 --> 00:32:35,481
Fine, let's say
your ridiculous theory is true.

551
00:32:35,481 --> 00:32:38,949
If he got married, built a family,
and had a kid, why come back?

552
00:32:38,949 --> 00:32:40,648
Why not just keep living that life?

553
00:32:40,648 --> 00:32:42,081
Because he couldn't stand not killing people?

554
00:32:42,081 --> 00:32:45,281
Or what, because he's some hero
who wants attention?

555
00:32:45,281 --> 00:32:48,514
Or maybe because life got boring?

556
00:32:49,314 --> 00:32:52,514
Why are you asking me?
Ask him yourself when you catch him.

557
00:32:52,514 --> 00:32:55,717
And ask him if he's really
a Baby Shark fanatic too.

558
00:32:55,717 --> 00:32:57,285
- Hey, you.
- Hey, who knows?

559
00:32:57,285 --> 00:33:00,681
That sticker might really have been a clue.

560
00:33:00,681 --> 00:33:02,881
<i>You never know.</i>

561
00:33:16,514 --> 00:33:17,748
Daddy, it's good.

562
00:33:17,748 --> 00:33:19,348
Is it good?

563
00:33:19,348 --> 00:33:21,414
I think it's delicious too.

564
00:33:23,548 --> 00:33:28,281
Yul, you can do this, right?

565
00:33:30,853 --> 00:33:32,414
I'll give it to you.

566
00:33:35,365 --> 00:33:36,781
Is it good?

567
00:33:36,781 --> 00:33:38,681
Yul, you learned how to do this, right?

568
00:33:38,681 --> 00:33:41,281
You're a big girl now,
so you can do it, right?

569
00:33:55,510 --> 00:33:57,573
[Yoo Bo Na's Relationship Chart]

570
00:34:07,584 --> 00:34:10,088
[Durumi Electronics Sales Team 3,
Killer Group]

571
00:35:40,614 --> 00:35:43,914
You're already awake? It's still early.

572
00:35:43,914 --> 00:35:45,648
I had a bad dream.

573
00:35:45,648 --> 00:35:50,548
I woke up and got scared
because you weren't there.

574
00:35:50,548 --> 00:35:52,781
A bad dream? What kind of dream?

575
00:35:52,781 --> 00:35:54,581
A dream where someone took you away.

576
00:35:54,581 --> 00:35:57,881
Who? Who took me?

577
00:35:57,881 --> 00:35:58,948
A monster.

578
00:35:58,948 --> 00:36:00,414
What? What is that?

579
00:36:00,414 --> 00:36:03,914
It's real. In my dream,
a really scary monster took you away.

580
00:36:03,914 --> 00:36:06,048
You're in big trouble now.

581
00:36:07,614 --> 00:36:12,548
No, maybe I'm the one who's in trouble.
I can't live without you.

582
00:36:12,548 --> 00:36:15,781
Then I guess I should sing
Baby Shark's Superhero for you.

583
00:36:15,781 --> 00:36:17,614
Apparently, it's the perfect weapon
against monsters.

584
00:36:17,614 --> 00:36:19,248
- Really?
- Yeah.

585
00:36:19,248 --> 00:36:20,648
Sing it.

586
00:36:20,648 --> 00:36:21,681
Sing it for me.

587
00:36:21,681 --> 00:36:26,048
Go back inside and get some more sleep.
I'll take Yul to daycare today.

588
00:36:33,948 --> 00:36:37,348
Let's just stay like this for one minute.

589
00:36:48,849 --> 00:36:51,704
[Durumi Electronics]

590
00:37:16,402 --> 00:37:18,369
Good morning!

591
00:38:37,461 --> 00:38:38,417
[Security Alert]

592
00:38:41,956 --> 00:38:45,689
Hey, when did Tae Min leave
without saying anything?

593
00:38:47,323 --> 00:38:49,823
[Unregistered Entrant Detected]
What, he brought someone with him?

594
00:38:51,889 --> 00:38:55,489
She's finally here! Our team's newbie!

595
00:38:56,423 --> 00:38:58,323
Wow!

596
00:39:00,056 --> 00:39:01,141
[Bong Tae Min]

597
00:39:05,215 --> 00:39:06,248
[Not Today]

598
00:39:06,248 --> 00:39:08,323
What? The case has been...

599
00:39:10,223 --> 00:39:12,189
The case has been closed?

600
00:39:14,289 --> 00:39:15,789
Just a moment.

601
00:39:17,489 --> 00:39:19,023
The investigation is already over?

602
00:39:19,023 --> 00:39:20,756
What about the NFS results?
Did they come out?

603
00:39:20,756 --> 00:39:24,123
They did come out,
but there was nothing significant.

604
00:39:24,123 --> 00:39:25,156
[Bae Doo Hyuk Car Explosion Case]

605
00:39:25,156 --> 00:39:28,923
It has been classified
as an accidental death.

606
00:39:28,923 --> 00:39:30,523
An accidental death?

607
00:39:30,523 --> 00:39:32,823
So you're saying it wasn't murder,
but an accident?

608
00:39:32,823 --> 00:39:37,423
Wow, our new employee
brought this on her first day.

609
00:39:37,423 --> 00:39:39,423
She's got great taste, right?

610
00:39:39,423 --> 00:39:40,523
Yeah.

611
00:39:40,523 --> 00:39:43,556
Then we should do proper introductions.

612
00:39:43,556 --> 00:39:46,023
As I've mentioned before,

613
00:39:46,023 --> 00:39:49,923
this is our new team member
who will be working with us, Ms. Oh Hyun Nam.

614
00:39:51,289 --> 00:39:54,423
Nice to meet you.
I look forward to working with you.

615
00:39:54,423 --> 00:39:56,056
Welcome!

616
00:39:58,989 --> 00:40:00,856
Same here. It's nice to meet you.

617
00:40:00,856 --> 00:40:04,840
Oh, Ms. Hyun Nam has been working alone
as a freelancer until now,

618
00:40:04,840 --> 00:40:07,304
so this is her first time working
in a team and company environment.

619
00:40:07,304 --> 00:40:09,356
Please help her out.

620
00:40:09,356 --> 00:40:11,889
Let me properly introduce everyone
on our team.

621
00:40:11,889 --> 00:40:14,756
This is Assistant Manager Yang Ye Sol.

622
00:40:14,756 --> 00:40:18,423
Her job is forging all kinds of documents.

623
00:40:18,423 --> 00:40:20,656
- How well?
- Perfectly.

624
00:40:20,656 --> 00:40:22,120
[Business Trip Application]
<i>Please come to me</i>

625
00:40:22,120 --> 00:40:23,289
<i>for anything related to paperwork.</i>

626
00:40:23,375 --> 00:40:26,091
[Destination: Musan, Reason: Client Meeting]

627
00:40:27,689 --> 00:40:29,256
Alright.

628
00:40:29,256 --> 00:40:30,589
You startled me.

629
00:40:30,589 --> 00:40:35,289
Were you there the whole time?
That's Manager Bong Tae Min.

630
00:40:35,289 --> 00:40:36,744
We don't call him Manager Bong, though.

631
00:40:36,744 --> 00:40:39,423
We call him Manager Tae or Manager Tae Min.

632
00:40:39,423 --> 00:40:43,389
He handles the cutting-edge equipment there.

633
00:40:44,823 --> 00:40:47,223
Well, that guy...

634
00:40:47,223 --> 00:40:49,223
Is he kept isolated separately?

635
00:40:49,223 --> 00:40:52,389
Isolated? Well, yeah.
It's more of self-isolation.

636
00:40:52,389 --> 00:40:55,423
None of us likes going into that room.

637
00:40:55,423 --> 00:40:57,256
You'll understand later.

638
00:41:00,823 --> 00:41:05,089
It's simple. No need for a long explanation.

639
00:41:05,089 --> 00:41:07,489
<i>A portable LPG gas canister,
burned completely black,</i>

640
00:41:07,489 --> 00:41:10,632
was found in the trunk of Bae Doo Hyuk's car.

641
00:41:10,632 --> 00:41:13,992
It turns out the valve was slightly open.

642
00:41:13,992 --> 00:41:15,789
This is...

643
00:41:15,789 --> 00:41:19,323
better known as Dr. Go.

644
00:41:19,323 --> 00:41:24,323
His job is making any death
look like a medical accident.

645
00:41:24,323 --> 00:41:25,423
How well?

646
00:41:25,423 --> 00:41:27,389
Perfectly.

647
00:41:27,389 --> 00:41:29,423
<i>I'm a real doctor.</i>

648
00:41:36,823 --> 00:41:39,256
The driver is going to the restroom.

649
00:41:39,256 --> 00:41:40,289
<i>Assistant Manager Ki Yeong Do.</i>

650
00:41:40,289 --> 00:41:44,323
Oh, he can do anything with computers.
He's our team's genius hacker.

651
00:41:45,256 --> 00:41:47,189
Nice to meet you.

652
00:41:47,189 --> 00:41:48,689
Yeah.

653
00:41:49,923 --> 00:41:53,423
Oh, I forgot to introduce myself.

654
00:41:53,423 --> 00:41:57,064
I'm Kim Bong Pal,

655
00:41:57,064 --> 00:42:00,889
the leader of Sales Team 3.

656
00:42:00,889 --> 00:42:05,423
My last name is actually Kim,
but everyone just calls me Team Leader Bong.

657
00:42:08,589 --> 00:42:10,289
What I do is...

658
00:42:15,556 --> 00:42:18,223
<i>You're saying there are
absolutely no signs of foul play?</i>

659
00:42:18,223 --> 00:42:21,923
<i>If someone put the gas tank in there
or deliberately opened the valve...</i>

660
00:42:21,923 --> 00:42:25,089
<i>Then there should've been footage of it.</i>

661
00:42:25,089 --> 00:42:27,956
<i>But we checked all the CCTV outside the club</i>

662
00:42:27,956 --> 00:42:30,723
<i>and all the dashcam footage
from the parking lot, and there's nothing.</i>

663
00:42:30,723 --> 00:42:33,389
<i>It was pure luck. A miracle.</i>

664
00:42:33,389 --> 00:42:36,856
<i>Well, there's usually a separate driver.</i>

665
00:42:36,856 --> 00:42:39,389
<i>But that day the driver
had a sudden stomach problem.</i>

666
00:42:39,389 --> 00:42:42,889
<i>Well, as for the gas tank,
Bae Doo Hyuk must've put it there himself.</i>

667
00:42:42,889 --> 00:42:45,156
<i>You know where Bae Doo Hyuk was going?</i>

668
00:42:45,156 --> 00:42:47,523
<i>His girlfriend was waiting
for him at a nearby villa.</i>

669
00:42:47,523 --> 00:42:50,523
<i>Maybe they were planning to have
a barbecue together or something.</i>

670
00:42:50,523 --> 00:42:53,289
<i>At least it happened
in a quiet suburban area.</i>

671
00:42:53,289 --> 00:42:55,323
<i>If it had happened downtown...</i>

672
00:42:55,323 --> 00:42:57,156
<i>Oh, dear.</i>

673
00:42:57,156 --> 00:42:59,956
Quiet location. Good.

674
00:42:59,956 --> 00:43:04,623
Once the taxi is more than
100 meters away, we'll go.

675
00:43:06,523 --> 00:43:09,756
Now, client meeting starts.

676
00:43:21,689 --> 00:43:23,489
Meeting clear.

677
00:43:25,023 --> 00:43:29,056
Rest in peace. I can't tell you to be reborn.

678
00:43:29,056 --> 00:43:32,923
Whether they die or survive,
I make it all look like an accident.

679
00:43:32,923 --> 00:43:34,956
How well? Perfectly.

680
00:43:34,956 --> 00:43:39,856
Simply put, you could say
he died an unfortunate death.

681
00:43:39,856 --> 00:43:41,689
<i>What a fate...</i>

682
00:43:42,356 --> 00:43:44,323
Isn't something a little strange?

683
00:43:44,323 --> 00:43:47,989
Everything lines up perfectly.
Like someone planned the whole thing.

684
00:43:47,989 --> 00:43:50,689
Bae Doo Hyuk wasn't just involved in drugs.

685
00:43:50,689 --> 00:43:55,056
He was known for framing his underlings
for murders he ordered.

686
00:43:55,056 --> 00:43:56,723
<i>It's a known fact in that world.</i>

687
00:43:56,723 --> 00:44:00,189
Who knows how many
other crimes he got away with?

688
00:44:00,189 --> 00:44:02,156
Exactly my point.
Which is why it is even more...

689
00:44:02,156 --> 00:44:03,323
<i>He was such a piece of work.</i>

690
00:44:03,323 --> 00:44:07,489
Honestly, a guy like him getting gunned down
by the Kingfisher is just unsurprising.

691
00:44:07,489 --> 00:44:09,656
Well, detectives speak with evidence,

692
00:44:09,656 --> 00:44:11,923
and you, the reporter,
should write with facts.

693
00:44:11,923 --> 00:44:15,623
<i>With everyone already worked up
over Kingfisher, who would even care?</i>

694
00:44:15,623 --> 00:44:19,089
Anyway, we've closed the case,
so just know that.

695
00:44:19,089 --> 00:44:21,384
And don't call me again.

696
00:44:21,384 --> 00:44:22,589
Hello...

697
00:44:22,589 --> 00:44:25,156
<i>But public sentiment is different.</i>

698
00:44:25,156 --> 00:44:28,423
<i>Because he only targets the worst criminals,</i>

699
00:44:28,423 --> 00:44:32,089
<i>some people are becoming
obsessed with Kingfisher.</i>

700
00:44:32,089 --> 00:44:34,889
<i>The Kingfisher fan club
already has over a million members.</i>

701
00:44:34,889 --> 00:44:36,323
<i>He targets the worst of the worst,</i>

702
00:44:36,323 --> 00:44:40,089
<i>especially those
who escaped proper punishment,</i>

703
00:44:40,089 --> 00:44:42,823
<i>so isn't it natural that people frustrated
with the flawed justice system</i>

704
00:44:42,823 --> 00:44:44,623
<i>are drawn to him?</i>

705
00:44:44,623 --> 00:44:49,023
<i>A powerful hero who punishes evil
in place of a powerless law.</i>

706
00:44:49,023 --> 00:44:52,089
Lastly, our ace.

707
00:44:52,089 --> 00:44:56,289
The face of Sales Team 3, Director Yoo Bo Na.

708
00:44:58,323 --> 00:44:59,756
As for Director Yoo...

709
00:44:59,756 --> 00:45:02,489
I know who she is.

710
00:45:12,856 --> 00:45:16,523
It's an honor to meet you, Kingfisher.

711
00:45:23,056 --> 00:45:26,689
The pleasure's mine, Ms. Oh Hyun Nam.

712
00:45:29,456 --> 00:45:32,956
Let's work well together from now on.

713
00:45:32,956 --> 00:45:34,456
"Together"?

714
00:45:38,423 --> 00:45:40,556
Yeah, let's work well together.

715
00:45:47,756 --> 00:45:48,856
Where's my desk?

716
00:45:48,856 --> 00:45:52,023
Oh, right here. Next to Assistant Manager Ki.

717
00:45:53,089 --> 00:45:56,489
All right, everyone. Back to work.

718
00:45:58,823 --> 00:46:00,523
Oh, right.

719
00:46:00,523 --> 00:46:02,756
I forgot to tell you what I do.

720
00:46:02,756 --> 00:46:04,356
Oh, you're right.

721
00:46:05,089 --> 00:46:06,756
I handle poisonings.

722
00:46:06,756 --> 00:46:10,344
Slip poison into food or drinks,
and no one ever knows perfectly.

723
00:46:14,189 --> 00:46:17,923
So, how about pork belly with water dropwort
for tonight's team dinner?

724
00:46:17,923 --> 00:46:19,023
Water dropwort is great for detoxing.

725
00:46:19,023 --> 00:46:20,223
Then make the arrangements.

726
00:46:20,223 --> 00:46:23,256
- Yeah, I'll book the place.
- Good.

727
00:46:35,656 --> 00:46:38,989
I've finished the article, so it's fine.

728
00:46:38,989 --> 00:46:44,189
I'll take care of Yul,
so don't worry and enjoy yourself.

729
00:46:44,189 --> 00:46:49,956
It's your welcome-back dinner too.
The guest of honor can't miss it.

730
00:46:49,956 --> 00:46:52,223
Then I'm counting on you tonight.

731
00:46:52,223 --> 00:46:54,923
When you get home,
wash Yul's hands and feet first, okay?

732
00:46:54,923 --> 00:46:58,223
And there's curry
and beef radish soup in the fridge...

733
00:46:58,223 --> 00:47:00,756
I can handle it.

734
00:47:01,956 --> 00:47:06,389
Okay, lecture over! I'll call you
when we're wrapping up.

735
00:47:06,389 --> 00:47:07,889
See you later.

736
00:47:13,736 --> 00:47:16,136
[Musan Drug Kingpin's
Car Explosion Ruled an Accident]

737
00:47:25,224 --> 00:47:26,224
[Musan Drug Kingpin's
Car Explosion Ruled an Accident]

738
00:47:29,023 --> 00:47:30,656
That's over, I see.

739
00:47:33,523 --> 00:47:34,856
Yeah, well, for now.

740
00:47:34,856 --> 00:47:37,923
"For now"? Does that mean
there's a second step?

741
00:47:37,923 --> 00:47:40,856
Forget it. From now on,
you're going after Kingfisher, right?

742
00:47:40,856 --> 00:47:42,923
"What did he do for 4 years,
and why did he come back without dying?"

743
00:47:42,923 --> 00:47:43,989
Well, something more in-depth.

744
00:47:43,989 --> 00:47:45,089
I'll get going.

745
00:47:45,089 --> 00:47:47,223
Oh, leaving already?

746
00:47:47,223 --> 00:47:50,323
Where to first? The NFS?
The crime scene? The police station?

747
00:47:50,323 --> 00:47:52,323
No. I'm picking up my daughter.

748
00:47:52,323 --> 00:47:54,489
- Your daughter?
- My wife is running late today.

749
00:47:54,489 --> 00:47:56,023
Oh, boy.

750
00:47:56,023 --> 00:47:57,823
I'll get going then.

751
00:47:57,823 --> 00:48:00,389
Hey, Tae Seong, you punk!

752
00:48:01,489 --> 00:48:03,016
Well, what's gotten into him?

753
00:48:03,016 --> 00:48:05,640
One bottle of soju, please!

754
00:48:07,123 --> 00:48:08,289
Dig in, everyone.

755
00:48:08,289 --> 00:48:10,089
Yeah.

756
00:48:10,089 --> 00:48:15,323
Director Yoo, don't you ever
get to eat meat at home or...

757
00:48:17,256 --> 00:48:22,523
We're more of a chicken family.
This pork is really amazing.

758
00:48:22,523 --> 00:48:25,956
The best part about coming back to work
is definitely the company dinners.

759
00:48:25,956 --> 00:48:29,536
Absolutely. Team dinners
are the best part of office life.

760
00:48:29,536 --> 00:48:30,536
That's true.

761
00:48:30,536 --> 00:48:32,056
- Alright.
- Cheers!

762
00:48:32,056 --> 00:48:34,089
Sales Team 3, fighting!

763
00:48:34,089 --> 00:48:37,064
- Fighting!
- Cheers!

764
00:48:42,356 --> 00:48:43,889
This is so good.

765
00:48:43,889 --> 00:48:44,923
Good, huh?

766
00:48:44,923 --> 00:48:46,723
Want a drink, Ms. Yoo?

767
00:48:49,123 --> 00:48:51,089
Oh, no!

768
00:48:51,089 --> 00:48:53,656
- Don't.
- I'll just smell it.

769
00:48:55,689 --> 00:48:58,589
Director Yoo hasn't touched alcohol
since she got married.

770
00:48:58,589 --> 00:49:04,756
Honestly, that's for the best.
She gets pretty wild when she drinks.

771
00:49:06,323 --> 00:49:09,189
By the way, I was really surprised.

772
00:49:09,189 --> 00:49:11,956
I heard that Hyun Nam
is the developer of that famous 'Mist'?

773
00:49:11,956 --> 00:49:13,956
Exactly.

774
00:49:13,956 --> 00:49:17,056
Now that Director Yoo is back

775
00:49:17,056 --> 00:49:18,523
and someone as talented
as Hyun Nam has joined us,

776
00:49:18,523 --> 00:49:22,989
Sales Team 3 is basically
the Avengers now, right?

777
00:49:22,989 --> 00:49:24,323
Absolutely.

778
00:49:24,323 --> 00:49:27,089
By the way, what exactly is 'Mist'?

779
00:49:27,089 --> 00:49:30,456
I guess you don't know about it,
Assistant Manager Yang.

780
00:49:33,889 --> 00:49:35,856
Gather around.

781
00:49:37,864 --> 00:49:44,723
Mist is the name of the poison
that's claimed the most lives

782
00:49:44,723 --> 00:49:46,789
in recent years.

783
00:49:46,789 --> 00:49:49,189
It's about 10,000 times
more toxic than arsenic

784
00:49:49,189 --> 00:49:52,623
and roughly 100 times
more potent than tetrodotoxin.

785
00:49:52,623 --> 00:49:57,589
No autopsy will ever detect a trace of it.

786
00:49:57,589 --> 00:50:02,589
By then, it naturally breaks down
and leaves almost no trace in the body.

787
00:50:02,589 --> 00:50:05,623
What do you think? Perfectly, right?

788
00:50:06,956 --> 00:50:11,489
For our line of work,
it's the perfect poison.

789
00:50:12,289 --> 00:50:14,456
That's incredible!

790
00:50:14,456 --> 00:50:17,089
How did you create something like that?

791
00:50:17,089 --> 00:50:19,489
Well, it just happened.

792
00:50:19,489 --> 00:50:21,356
"Well, it just happened."

793
00:50:22,889 --> 00:50:24,256
But I'm curious.

794
00:50:24,256 --> 00:50:27,189
With skills like yours,
you could've stayed independent.

795
00:50:27,856 --> 00:50:30,723
Why join this team?

796
00:50:32,856 --> 00:50:33,856
Hold on.

797
00:50:33,856 --> 00:50:35,389
Oh, Director Yoo!

798
00:50:37,989 --> 00:50:40,423
I have a debt to repay.

799
00:50:44,223 --> 00:50:45,256
What did you do today, Yul?

800
00:50:45,256 --> 00:50:47,056
<i>Ta-da!</i>

801
00:50:47,056 --> 00:50:49,089
<i>I drew Mommy and Daddy, and Yul.</i>

802
00:50:49,089 --> 00:50:51,323
Wow, that's a great drawing, Yul!

803
00:50:51,323 --> 00:50:53,689
But why did you draw Daddy better?

804
00:50:53,689 --> 00:50:59,289
<i>Because Yul loves Daddy more, right?</i>

805
00:50:59,289 --> 00:51:03,432
No, Yul loves Mommy more, right?
You love Mommy more, don't you?

806
00:51:03,432 --> 00:51:09,448
<i>No. I love both Mommy and Daddy.</i>

807
00:51:10,423 --> 00:51:15,456
I love Yul too. Love you! Heart!

808
00:51:15,456 --> 00:51:16,923
I'll be home soon.

809
00:51:16,923 --> 00:51:19,856
<i>See you later, Mommy!</i>

810
00:51:21,156 --> 00:51:22,356
So cute.

811
00:51:22,356 --> 00:51:25,023
It's a shame no one else
gets to see it, Kingfisher.

812
00:51:25,023 --> 00:51:27,656
You're having all the fun by yourself.

813
00:51:36,189 --> 00:51:39,256
Don't worry. No one would believe it anyway.

814
00:51:39,256 --> 00:51:44,023
Who'd ever imagine
the infamous Kingfisher is a married mom?

815
00:51:57,623 --> 00:52:00,789
Hyun Nam, do you have Mist?

816
00:52:02,856 --> 00:52:08,889
No, not the drinkable kind, the spray kind.
My clothes smell like pork barbecue.

817
00:52:08,889 --> 00:52:10,440
Got any?

818
00:52:10,440 --> 00:52:12,040
Oh, gosh.

819
00:52:18,923 --> 00:52:21,523
A lot of people would be disappointed.

820
00:52:21,523 --> 00:52:23,656
You're practically worshiped as a hero.

821
00:52:23,656 --> 00:52:26,589
If they found out you're living
such an ordinary family life...

822
00:52:26,589 --> 00:52:28,489
You think so?

823
00:52:28,489 --> 00:52:33,156
Have you ever wished you could
go back to your old life?

824
00:52:35,189 --> 00:52:37,923
Even married women say
they think that sometimes.

825
00:52:37,923 --> 00:52:42,856
Like wanting to go back to the carefree,
glamorous days of being single.

826
00:52:43,489 --> 00:52:47,356
Not at all. I like my life now.

827
00:52:48,589 --> 00:52:52,189
Because everything
that matters to me is right here.

828
00:52:53,289 --> 00:52:55,489
I see.

829
00:52:55,489 --> 00:52:57,056
Then why did you come back?

830
00:52:57,056 --> 00:52:59,556
You could've just kept living
that happy little life.

831
00:52:59,556 --> 00:53:01,989
Then why did you join this team, Hyun Nam?

832
00:53:01,989 --> 00:53:04,423
Did you come here to see me?

833
00:53:04,423 --> 00:53:08,123
Well, it just seemed like
you've been watching me all night.

834
00:53:08,123 --> 00:53:12,389
I wondered if you were my fan.
Or maybe an anti-fan?

835
00:53:12,389 --> 00:53:16,589
They say former fans
make the scariest haters.

836
00:53:16,589 --> 00:53:19,856
That's a little childish.

837
00:53:25,923 --> 00:53:30,389
Oh Hyun Nam, everyone makes choices.

838
00:53:30,389 --> 00:53:33,823
Those choices shape a person's life.

839
00:53:33,823 --> 00:53:36,680
Everyone makes
what they believe is the best choice

840
00:53:36,680 --> 00:53:38,989
because their life matters to them.

841
00:53:38,989 --> 00:53:42,856
And I think those choices deserve respect.

842
00:53:42,856 --> 00:53:44,623
I'm not here to listen to lectures...

843
00:53:44,623 --> 00:53:50,789
Just like it was your own choice
to do this work and join this company.

844
00:53:50,789 --> 00:53:55,056
No one forced you in
or pushed you out, right?

845
00:54:00,156 --> 00:54:04,389
If you're looking to play hero,
you've come to the wrong place.

846
00:54:04,389 --> 00:54:07,489
That's for Baby Sharks.

847
00:54:07,489 --> 00:54:09,223
Not us.

848
00:54:11,323 --> 00:54:13,089
What if...

849
00:54:14,056 --> 00:54:18,023
What would you do if you lost
the things that matter most to you?

850
00:54:20,123 --> 00:54:21,623
I don't know.

851
00:54:22,556 --> 00:54:24,589
I've never thought about it.

852
00:54:25,256 --> 00:54:27,189
Because I don't believe
that will ever happen.

853
00:54:43,189 --> 00:54:45,723
[Caller ID Restricted:
I'd like to provide a tip about Kingfisher]

854
00:55:13,005 --> 00:55:14,338
May I take your order?

855
00:55:14,338 --> 00:55:17,305
One iced Americano, please.

856
00:55:22,405 --> 00:55:25,805
<i>Are you going to be late today?
I'm finishing early today.</i>

857
00:55:26,671 --> 00:55:28,138
<i>Really?</i>

858
00:55:28,138 --> 00:55:31,071
<i>I just have one meeting with an informant,
and then I'll be done too.</i>

859
00:55:32,105 --> 00:55:34,738
<i>Then how about we go on a date for a change?</i>

860
00:55:34,738 --> 00:55:38,171
<i>Se Ah said she'll watch Yul.
Guess she could use a little spending money.</i>

861
00:55:40,038 --> 00:55:44,171
<i>Of course, it's okay with me.
As expected, the power of pocket money!</i>

862
00:55:47,905 --> 00:55:49,505
Thanks!

863
00:56:06,538 --> 00:56:07,771
Alright!

864
00:56:07,771 --> 00:56:12,605
Today is your last chance to take it easy,
so head home early.

865
00:56:12,605 --> 00:56:16,871
And you all know vacation days
are off the table for a while, right?

866
00:56:16,871 --> 00:56:20,338
So get some rest while you can.

867
00:56:20,338 --> 00:56:22,271
Good work. Get home safely.

868
00:56:22,271 --> 00:56:23,805
Yes, sir.

869
00:56:26,238 --> 00:56:28,505
But Oh Hyun Nam is something else.

870
00:56:28,505 --> 00:56:31,638
Taking a personal day
on her second day of work.

871
00:56:32,805 --> 00:56:35,038
She must've had something urgent.

872
00:56:35,038 --> 00:56:39,738
Let's let it slide this time.

873
00:56:40,838 --> 00:56:42,571
Yeah.

874
00:56:42,571 --> 00:56:44,105
Go home, everyone.

875
00:57:05,805 --> 00:57:07,162
[Honey, I've arrived. When will you get here?
Where are you, Tae Seong?]

876
00:57:10,099 --> 00:57:11,519
[New Message]

877
00:57:23,354 --> 00:57:26,738
Well, Assistant Manager Ki,
why are you still here?

878
00:57:28,738 --> 00:57:32,371
What have you been working on all day?

879
00:57:32,371 --> 00:57:36,871
I figured out
why Oh Hyun Nam joined our team.

880
00:57:38,138 --> 00:57:39,871
What are you talking about?

881
00:57:40,738 --> 00:57:41,905
Oh, Director Yoo!

882
00:57:41,905 --> 00:57:43,171
Ms. Yoo, you came just in time.

883
00:57:43,171 --> 00:57:44,738
- Oh Hyun Nam...
- Please track where this message came from.

884
00:57:44,738 --> 00:57:46,338
As fast as you can.

885
00:57:49,871 --> 00:57:55,071
What is this? What's going on?
What about Oh Hyun Nam?

886
00:57:55,071 --> 00:57:58,838
<i>See if you can find me. But come alone.</i>

887
00:57:58,838 --> 00:58:01,038
<i>If you're not here before eight,
whatever happens is on you.</i>

888
00:58:01,038 --> 00:58:02,605
It's for Bo Na.

889
00:58:04,171 --> 00:58:06,338
She came to meet her.

890
00:58:13,071 --> 00:58:14,838
What do you mean?

891
00:58:35,071 --> 00:58:38,571
[Archived Portraits]
Oh Hyun Nam. Real name, Oh Seung Ah.

892
00:58:38,571 --> 00:58:40,271
<i>Fifteen years ago, in winter,</i>

893
00:58:40,271 --> 00:58:43,671
<i>Oh Seung Ah's dad, Oh Man Seok,
was released from prison.</i>

894
00:58:43,671 --> 00:58:46,471
<i>He went straight to see his daughter.</i>

895
00:58:46,471 --> 00:58:48,705
<i>That Christmas night,</i>

896
00:58:50,105 --> 00:58:52,971
<i>Bo Na killed Oh Seung Ah's dad.</i>

897
00:58:53,771 --> 00:58:56,038
<i>Right in front of her.</i>

898
00:58:58,038 --> 00:58:59,571
So...

899
00:59:00,671 --> 00:59:03,805
Oh Hyun Nam deliberately joined Sales Team 3

900
00:59:04,571 --> 00:59:08,138
to get close to Director Yoo
and avenge her dad's death?

901
00:59:25,738 --> 00:59:29,971
Sometimes I wondered
if that day would ever come.

902
00:59:29,971 --> 00:59:32,471
That someone might find me.

903
00:59:33,471 --> 00:59:35,838
That someone might come looking for me.

904
00:59:35,838 --> 00:59:37,371
Who?

905
00:59:40,905 --> 00:59:43,205
I hope it doesn't happen.

906
01:00:50,505 --> 01:00:52,371
Where's Kwon Tae Seong?

907
01:00:53,671 --> 01:00:56,071
You ignored the photos,

908
01:00:56,071 --> 01:00:59,471
but the second I touched your husband,
you came running, huh?

909
01:00:59,471 --> 01:01:03,771
Where is he? I won't ask a third time.

910
01:01:09,005 --> 01:01:11,871
This is called Mist S.

911
01:01:13,671 --> 01:01:17,138
Drink 3 milliliters,
and in about five minutes you'll fall asleep.

912
01:01:17,138 --> 01:01:20,005
A sleep you'll never wake up from.

913
01:01:20,671 --> 01:01:23,405
I gave Kwon Tae Seong 6 milliliters.

914
01:01:27,205 --> 01:01:29,471
Have you lost your mind?

915
01:01:29,471 --> 01:01:31,338
Do you have any idea
how much that stuff costs?

916
01:01:31,338 --> 01:01:35,371
What's the price on your head?
Want in on this bill too?

917
01:01:40,305 --> 01:01:45,305
If he doesn't get the antidote
within the next hour, he'll die.

918
01:01:46,205 --> 01:01:49,938
You know exactly what that means, right?

919
01:01:54,671 --> 01:01:56,671
What do you want?

920
01:02:01,705 --> 01:02:03,638
Do you know who I am?

921
01:02:04,705 --> 01:02:06,205
I do.

922
01:02:07,571 --> 01:02:09,071
You do?

923
01:02:10,205 --> 01:02:13,105
I knew you'd figure it out.

924
01:02:14,938 --> 01:02:17,571
Or is that the work of that rude hacker?

925
01:02:19,638 --> 01:02:21,771
I know exactly who you are.

926
01:02:31,438 --> 01:02:33,838
Do you want to kill my husband?

927
01:02:44,071 --> 01:02:45,838
Then kill me too.

928
01:03:38,090 --> 01:03:40,881
[A Bona Fide Killer]

929
01:03:40,905 --> 01:03:42,338
Under no circumstances

930
01:03:42,338 --> 01:03:44,605
can we meet with anyone
other than the client.

931
01:03:44,605 --> 01:03:47,905
Because you messed with someone
you never should have.

932
01:03:47,905 --> 01:03:49,705
Things had been quiet for a while.

933
01:03:49,705 --> 01:03:51,205
- They said they saw Kingfisher?
- You're about to see

934
01:03:51,205 --> 01:03:52,938
another side of Kingfisher.

935
01:03:52,938 --> 01:03:55,105
You know the whole sales team workshop
is scheduled, right?

936
01:03:55,105 --> 01:03:58,338
There's a strong possibility their base
of operations is somewhere nearby.

937
01:03:58,338 --> 01:04:00,538
These punks are crossing the line.

938
01:04:00,538 --> 01:04:02,905
It's 300 million won per head!

939
01:04:02,905 --> 01:04:04,571
I think we're really going to die.

940
01:04:04,571 --> 01:04:06,938
Why isn't Mommy answering?

941
01:04:07,771 --> 01:04:09,338
Mom and Dad...

942
01:04:09,338 --> 01:04:11,171
Director Yoo is awake.

943
01:04:11,171 --> 01:04:12,238
Never lose their dignity...

944
01:04:12,238 --> 01:04:14,771
Those darn flies won't stop buzzing.

945
01:04:14,771 --> 01:04:16,838
Maybe I should go deal with them.
